<title>USA: U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Census Bureau reports factory consumption of domestic and foreign cotton (bales):</p>
<p>    Nov 96-B   Oct 96-A    Nov 95   Cum 1996   Cum 1995</p>
<p>     816,704    829,329   761,391  8,643,706  9,610,057</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE CONSUMPTION OF ALL COTTON (bales):</p>
<p>    Nov 96-Y   Oct 96-X   Nov 95</p>
<p>	40,836     41,467   38,453</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE SPINDLE HOURS OPERATED:</p>
<p>    Nov 96-X  Oct 96-Y   Nov 95</p>
<p>	   146	 149	158</p>
<p>A-4 weeks. B-4 weeks. X-Based on 20 days. Y-20 days.</p>
</text>
